blk2,n=re.subn(r'<p><b>A giving Tuesday in the foothills\.</b>.*?</p>','<p><b>An evening to pour, after a giving Tuesday.</b> Today in the Foothills is built only from the events database&#8217;s published feed, the same feed the public events viewer reads — <b>four in-beat events span today</b>, listed below as cards, verified against the feed this evening. The <b>Sierra Oak Farms veggie stand</b> (featured first, at Dave&#8217;s direction) sold its <b>last day</b> at Fiddletown Rd and Mt. Whitney; the <b>Rotary Club packed Thanksgiving boxes</b> at the Amador County Fairgrounds in Plymouth at 8:00 AM; <b>Baked in Amador&#8217;s Thanksgiving preorder pickup</b> ran until 3:00 PM in Volcano and returns Wednesday; and the evening&#8217;s remaining event, <b>Tapas Tuesday at Krissie Vineyards</b> (which entered the database this afternoon), pours on Shenandoah Rd in Plymouth <b>until 7:00 PM</b> — mind the dogs logged on Shenandoah Rd at Bell Rd (see the Safety Wire). <b>Tomorrow, Wed Nov 25, in the database:</b> Preschool Story Time at the Plymouth Library, 1:00 PM; Amador All Stars at Feist Wines, Drytown; Friendsgiving at the Plymouth Hotel Kitchen &amp; Bar, 6:30 PM, and the Friendsgiving Show in Placerville, 7:00 PM; and Luka&#8217;s Thanksgiving box-dinner pickup in Jackson (see The Week Ahead).</p>',blk,count=1,flags=re.S)
